The debloat list in this directory is `uad_lists.json.gz`, a gzipped copy of
`resources/assets/uad_lists.json` from the Universal Android Debloater Next
Generation project:

    https://github.com/Universal-Debloater-Alliance/universal-android-debloater-next-generation

Upstream states that the project is licensed under the GNU General Public
License, version 3:

    https://github.com/Universal-Debloater-Alliance/universal-android-debloater-next-generation/blob/main/LICENSE

adbshare is distributed under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or
later, so this data can be redistributed as part of it.

What the file is
----------------

A map of Android package name to a short description of the app, which
curated list it belongs to (aosp, carrier, google, misc, oem), which other
packages it depends on, and how safe it is to remove:

    Recommended  safe to remove
    Advanced    breaks obscure or minor parts of functionality
    Expert      breaks widespread functionality, but should not boot-loop
    Unsafe      can break vital parts of the operating system

The `removal` level is upstream's own risk assessment and is reproduced
verbatim, along with the descriptions. Both are the upstream authors' work
and are covered by the licence above.

How it is refreshed
-------------------

The file is a snapshot. To take a newer one:

    make debloat-list

which downloads the current upstream file and compresses it in place. Nothing
in adbshare edits it: it is read as it is found.
